      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here are some arguments you can use to push back against the new carbon emission standards: \n\nFirstly, highlight the economic concerns, such as the potential job losses and increased costs to your business, which may lead to reduced production or even factory closures. Additionally, you can emphasize the impact on other Ohio-based industries, e.g., automotive, which would be disproportionately affected by the new regulations. \n\nAnother argument is that the standards may push your business overseas where carbon emission regulations are less stringent, resulting in a loss of Ohio jobs. Furthermore, point out the effectiveness of existing regulations and the need for more targeted and efficient solutions rather than broader, more punitive measures.",
